"""Portable local review, no external resources or network dependencies."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html,zipfile,hashlib
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
components=[
 ('FWS','1. Facility-water boundary','The green lines connect the CDU to the facility heat-rejection plant. For this study only, facility water enters at 25 C and returns near 35 C. We have not selected a chiller, dry cooler or site climate. The facility fluid stays separate from rack coolant.',[32,365,132,205]),
 ('HX-101','2. CDU heat exchanger','Transfers the rack heat into the facility loop without mixing the two fluids. Start at 1 MW heat transfer, then add pump heat. Its UA, terminal temperature approaches, pressure-loss curves and fouling allowance must be selected together. The 3D block is a packaging envelope.',[165,315,145,295]),
 ('EV-101','3. Expansion, pressure reference and fill','Connects near pump suction. Accommodates coolant expansion and establishes fill pressure; it does not supply the circulating pump head. Vessel size, precharge, fill/backflow protection and operating pressure are pending. Check high-point absolute pressure and pump NPSH later.',[263,150,133,143]),
 ('P-101','4. Variable-speed pump bank','P-101A and B are duty pumps; C is standby. Each duty pump initially targets 43.4 m3/h at the same head, approximately 27.5 m from Stage 01 presizing. Head does not divide by two. Actual curves, speed range, motor power and standby delay will be tested in OpenModelica.',[383,247,344,346]),
 ('Pump valves','5. Pump isolation and check valves','Each pump branch has inlet/outlet isolation for maintenance and a discharge check valve to limit reverse circulation through a stopped pump. The QET diagram shows these functions. Most valve internals and the check-valve bodies are not detailed in the first 3D layout.',[428,288,269,268]),
 ('F-101','6. Duplex filtration','Removes debris before coolant reaches narrow rack passages. Two filter legs allow a service arrangement with one available path; there is no uncontrolled open bypass in this concept. Differential-pressure monitoring detects loading. Clean/dirty loss curves and switchover details are still required.',[780,214,157,173]),
 ('H-101','7. Supply header','Blue is nominal 35 C coolant. The 125 mm clear-ID header feeds ten parallel 40 mm-ID rack branch pairs. As water leaves each supply tee, header flow decreases. We must model each segment rather than applying full module flow everywhere.',[1010,270,230,134]),
 ('Racks','8. Ten parallel rack branches','Each rack represents 100 kW transferred to liquid and a target 144.7 L/min for a 10 K temperature rise. Sheet 02 shows supply isolation, flow indication, equivalent rack/cold-plate resistance, balancing and return isolation. The assumed rack loss is 100 kPa at design flow; OEM curves will replace it.',[1092,416,177,186]),
 ('H-102','9. Return header','Orange is nominal 45 C return coolant. Rack streams join the return header and flow back to HX-101. This is a direct-return baseline: rack branch drops are similar, but common header path lengths differ. A reverse-return comparison will follow; equal branch length does not guarantee equal flow.',[794,711,421,62]),
 ('Sensors','10. Measurements and future control','FT measures total flow; rack FI points monitor distribution. TT-S/R track temperatures, PT-S/D track pump suction and discharge, filter PDT tracks fouling, and the critical-rack PDT will guide variable-speed control. Dashed lines are instrument connections, not coolant pipes. No controller has been simulated yet.',[1274,380,107,194]),
 ('Protection','11. Vent, drain, relief and leak detection','Sheet 02 includes a high-point vent, and Sheet 01 includes a low-point drain and a relief concept to safe collection. Relief setpoint, trapped-liquid protection, pressure ratings, leak-sensor positions and containment still need detailed engineering. No pressure qualification follows from the displayed wall thickness.',[966,146,347,82]),
]
svg=(B/'diagram/01-system-piping.svg').read_text()
hits=''.join(f'<rect class="hit" data-component="{i}" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="{html.escape(c[1])}" x="{c[3][0]}" y="{c[3][1]}" width="{c[3][2]}" height="{c[3][3]}" />' for i,c in enumerate(components))
svg=svg.replace('</svg>',hits+'</svg>')
css='''*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;color:#17394d;background:#eef4f6;font:16px/1.55 system-ui}header,main{max-width:1600px;margin:auto;padding:24px}header{padding-bottom:8px}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.15;margin:8px 0}h2{font-size:23px;line-height:1.25}p{max-width:1050px}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.13em;color:#38778a}.status{padding:12px 16px;background:#fff6df;border-left:4px solid #be8e34}.tabs,.viewbuttons,.downloads{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:18px 0}button,.downloads a{font:inherit;padding:9px 15px;border:1px solid #c7d9e1;border-radius:7px;background:white;color:#17394d;cursor:pointer;text-decoration:none}button[aria-selected=true],button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#17394d;color:white}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible,.hit:focus{outline:3px solid #be8e34}.workspace{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,3fr) minmax(280px,1fr);gap:20px}.drawing,aside,.panel{background:white;border:1px solid #dce6eb;border-radius:10px;padding:18px}.drawing{padding:0;overflow:auto}.drawing svg,.drawing img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.hit{fill:transparent;stroke:transparent;stroke-width:3;cursor:pointer}.hit:hover,.hit.active{fill:#e7b96320;stroke:#c28c2c}.component-list{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px}.component-list button{font-size:12px;padding:5px 8px}.hint{color:#5f7786;font-size:13px}.legend{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}.legend b{padding-left:14px;border-left:8px solid #167bac}.legend b.hot{border-color:#cb552d}.legend b.green{border-color:#307d67}[hidden]{display:none!important}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{text-align:left;padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce6eb}.panel{margin-top:20px}code{font-size:13px}footer{margin:28px 0;color:#5f7786;font-size:13px}@media(max-width:950px){.workspace{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:29px}.drawing{min-height:0}header,main{padding:16px}.component-list button{font-size:14px}}'''
buttons=''.join(f'<button data-select="{i}" aria-pressed="{str(i==0).lower()}">{html.escape(c[0])}</button>' for i,c in enumerate(components))
doc=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Data-center piping and layout R1 | Khani Solutions</title><style>{css}</style><body>
<header><p class="eyebrow">KHANI SOLUTIONS / DATA-CENTER HYDRAULICS / DESIGN REVIEW R1</p><h1>Follow the water. Inspect the layout.</h1><p>A tagged QElectroTech piping diagram and native FreeCAD layout built on Intel. Ten 100 kW liquid-cooled racks, a separate facility circuit, and a three-pump CDU concept.</p><p class="status">Design stage only. No project-specific hydraulic or thermal solve yet. Geometry, pressure losses and equipment envelopes are provisional. Review this arrangement before we build the OpenModelica network.</p></header>
<main><nav class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Design views"><button role="tab" id="tab-system" aria-controls="system" aria-selected="true" data-tab="system">1. System piping</button><button role="tab" id="tab-branches" aria-controls="branches" aria-selected="false" data-tab="branches">2. Rack branches</button><button role="tab" id="tab-layout" aria-controls="layout" aria-selected="false" data-tab="layout">3. FreeCAD layout</button></nav>
<section id="system" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-system"><div class="workspace"><div class="drawing">{svg}</div><aside><p class="eyebrow">STEP BY STEP</p><div class="component-list">{buttons}</div><div id="explanation" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="hint">Select a component in the drawing or use the buttons above. Blue arrows show supply, orange shows return. Arrow lengths do not encode flow magnitude.</p></aside></div></section>
<section id="branches" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-branches" hidden><div class="drawing"><img src="diagram/02-rack-branches.svg" alt="Ten parallel rack branches with supply isolation, flow indication, rack heat load, balancing and return isolation"></div><p>Follow any branch downward: supply header → isolation valve → flow measurement → rack cold plates → balancing valve → return isolation → return header. Valves and QDs require vendor curves and service details.</p></section>
<section id="layout" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-layout" hidden><div class="viewbuttons" role="group" aria-label="FreeCAD camera"><button data-camera="isometric" aria-pressed="true">Isometric</button><button data-camera="top" aria-pressed="false">Top / floor plan</button><button data-camera="elevation" aria-pressed="false">Front elevation</button></div><div class="drawing"><img id="cad-image" src="review/layout-isometric.png" alt="Native FreeCAD isometric view of the ten-rack cooling layout"></div><p class="legend"><b>35 C supply</b><b class="hot">45 C return</b><b class="green">Facility / expansion connections</b></p><p>20 × 8 m planning envelope. Racks are 0.8 × 1.2 × 2.2 m at 1.2 m pitch. Header centerlines are 2.70 m above the floor over the rear service aisle. The CDU skeleton shows the exchanger, pump bank, filter envelope and expansion vessel. Service zones and supports are conceptual; they do not establish code compliance or structural sizing.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>What changes from Stage 01?</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Stage 01 presizing</th><th>This routing concept</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Main supply + return headers</td><td>40 m placeholder</td><td>24.40 m straight external headers, plus CDU links and internal pipework itemized in the schedule</td></tr><tr><td>One rack branch pair</td><td>20 m placeholder</td><td>4.747 m routed branch centerline, excluding rack internals / connections represented by equipment resistance</td></tr><tr><td>Header / branch clear ID</td><td>125 / 40 mm</td><td>Retained as starting diameters; not final selected pipe sizes</td></tr><tr><td>Pump head</td><td>Approximately 27.5 m</td><td>Not recalculated yet; network solve must use these routes and updated component curves</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="hint">The 2.70 m elevation changes local static pressure. In a filled, closed equal-density loop it does not add 2.70 m of net circulation head. Check fill pressure, component ratings and NPSH separately.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Open the actual working files</h2><div class="downloads"><a href="diagram/DataCenter_Piping_R1.qet" download>QElectroTech project</a><a href="cad/DataCenter_Layout_R1.FCStd" download>Native FreeCAD model</a><a href="cad/DataCenter_Layout_R1.step" download>STEP assembly</a><a href="cad/pipe-route-schedule.csv" download>Pipe route schedule</a><a href="Stage-02-Design-R1.zip" download>Complete design package</a><a href="diagram/01-system-piping.svg">Full-size system diagram</a><a href="verification/native-reopen-verification.json">CAD verification</a></div><p>The QET project contains two editable folios built from native drawing primitives. It is a graphical piping diagram, not an electrical netlist or solver model. FreeCAD contains 285 valid positive-volume solid objects, verified after reopening; STEP import is also checked. The native assembly has editable objects and metadata; rerun the included macro to regenerate route geometry after changing its parameters.</p><p>Pipe walls are illustrative 4 mm (headers) and 3 mm (rack branches), not pressure-qualified. Tee intersections are layout joins; bores have not been combined into a continuous CFD fluid volume. Catalog selection, detailed safety/service design and interference checks remain future work.</p></section><footer>Mohammadreza Khani, PhD · Independent concept design · R1 · 23 October 2026 · Next: review routing, then solve the segmented OpenModelica hydraulic network.</footer></main>
<script>const components={json.dumps(components)};
function selectComponent(i){{document.getElementById('explanation').replaceChildren();let h=document.createElement('h2'),p=document.createElement('p');h.textContent=components[i][1];p.textContent=components[i][2];document.getElementById('explanation').append(h,p);document.querySelectorAll('[data-select]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(+b.dataset.select===i)));document.querySelectorAll('.hit').forEach(b=>b.classList.toggle('active',+b.dataset.component===i));}}
document.querySelectorAll('[data-select]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>selectComponent(+b.dataset.select));document.querySelectorAll('.hit').forEach(b=>{{b.onclick=()=>selectComponent(+b.dataset.component);b.onkeydown=e=>{{if(e.key==='Enter'||e.key===' '){{e.preventDefault();selectComponent(+b.dataset.component);}}}};}});
document.querySelectorAll('[data-tab]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{{document.querySelectorAll('[role=tabpanel]').forEach(s=>s.hidden=s.id!==b.dataset.tab);document.querySelectorAll('[data-tab]').forEach(t=>t.setAttribute('aria-selected',String(t===b)));}});
document.querySelectorAll('[data-camera]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{{document.getElementById('cad-image').src='review/layout-'+b.dataset.camera+'.png';document.getElementById('cad-image').alt='Native FreeCAD '+b.dataset.camera+' view of the cooling layout';document.querySelectorAll('[data-camera]').forEach(t=>t.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(t===b)));}});selectComponent(0);</script></body></html>'''
(B/'Review.html').write_text(doc)
print('Built portable local design review.')
